id=a52sxq_tethering_trains
name=Galaxy A52s 5G: Tethering train BPF coverage guard
author=kusti420
description=Our BPF loader is frozen: it always loads /system/etc/bpf/a52_netd.o, whatever Tethering APEX Google Play has activated, and that APEX's system_server/netd code aborts if a map or program pin its own netd.o defines is missing (crash loop; apexd reverts a fresh update, but a ROM flashed under an already active train has no such safety net). known/ holds the netd.o of the factory Tethering and of every Play train seen in the field (<versionCode>_<label>_netd.o). The build aborts unless a52_netd.o defines every map of each of them with the same definition (ringbuf min_kver lowered to 5.4 by regen.py and 5.10+-only maps excepted) and pins every program they would pin on 5.4.302 at API 37, so a regenerated a52_netd.o can never silently drop a train that phones already run. Ships the list as /system/etc/bpf/a52_netd.known for k4-mainline-diag. New train: copy its netd.o (/apex/com.android.tethering/etc/bpf/mainline/netd.o, or /cache/k4_mainline/staged_tethering_netd.o after a rolled-back update boot) into known/, rerun tethering/regen.py --train-progs with it, rebuild.
